  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The question asks for a mean-state bias, RMSE and spatial correlation against WOA23 on the WOA23 1-degree grid, which requires putting models and WOA23 on one grid and using a single mask over all of them, while keeping WOA23's land-sea mask out of comparisons that do not involve WOA23.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all three models and WOA23 on the one 1° grid, build a single mask with `build_comparison_mask` (`ocean_only=True`, valid here because WOA23 is in the comparison), apply `.where(mask)` to every field before bias, RMSE and pattern correlation, and report the mask's cell counts alongside the metrics.",
        "Do not score or rank the models on separate pairwise cells: each pair would cover a different piece of ocean, so the scores would not be comparable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "historical-ssp245-member-continuity",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/historical-ssp245-member-continuity.md",
      "sha256": "02341c56015c6296db14585b4561fc32ca6b4e52e2264bec50eee6746c1d55f6",
      "reason": "The question explicitly asks for caveats arising from the ensemble members used for each model's two experiments, and this fragment states that local CESM2 ssp245 (r10i1p1f1) continues a different member than the local CESM2 historical (r1i1p1f1), mixing forced change with internal variability.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "CESM2 historical r1 and ssp245 r10 are different realisations, so its delta SSS contains forced change plus the internal-variability difference between two members, and its ssp245/historical slope ratio compares two different members — state this; GFDL-ESM4 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are r1/r1 and continuous.",
        "Do not fit a trend across the 2015 join for CESM2; historical and ssp245 slopes are fitted separately."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices.md",
      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The mean-state bias must be taken against the observed WOA23 1971-2000 climatology (an observed baseline, which keeps the bias), and the delta SSS compares means from two different periods, so the rule that anomalies are defined only relative to their baseline applies.",
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "not_applicable_reason": "no anomaly, climate-index or seasonal-convention comparison is made; the SSS bias is a direct difference from the WOA23 1971-2000 normal and the trends are of annual means."
    },
    {
      "id": "serial-correlation-and-significance",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/serial-correlation-and-significance.md",
      "sha256": "fe11bd008257a589f44e369faba5fa31ab3cf9ad99280e88c763ac45d2b0e917",
      "reason": "The question requires trend confidence intervals, R-squared, an exclude-zero statement, and stippling of cells with p < 0.05, and this fragment warns that autocorrelated monthly/neighbouring ocean series need an effective sample size and that a trend question needs an explicit straight-line fit quoted with its interval.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Fit with `method='linear'` (`fit_1D_trend`, `fit_trend_map`), which applies an effective sample size along time by default; quote the corrected 95% CI, R² and whether the interval excludes zero.",
        "Draw the slope everywhere and stipple the significant cells rather than blanking the insignificant ones; for the spatial pattern correlation read the coefficient, not its p-value."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The delta SSS is requested for Atlantic, Indian and Pacific basins with marginal seas folded in and Southern/Arctic excluded, so the fragment's point that basin statistics depend on which partition is used, and must say so, applies.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Basin means use the WOA23 basin mask via `select_basin` with `include_marginal_seas=True` and `depth_dependent=False` (surface labels) for the 0-10 m SSS; state that the WOA labelling, not the OMIP 10-region mask, was used.",
        "The Ofx `basin` variable is not in the local archive; each mask choice changes basin means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-so-practical-salinity",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-so-practical-salinity.md",
      "sha256": "96f2763290996040d675ca6e8f997ea29fa320b8f6e6793bf2c6fcb739345e19",
      "reason": "SSS is to be reported in psu, and this fragment fixes how CMIP6 salinity is treated (Practical Salinity, \"0.001\" meaning parts per thousand) and what TEOS-10 conversions require.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Model `so` and WOA23 salinity are both practical salinity: difference them directly, with no unit conversion — the `0.001` units string already denotes psu-scale numbers, so map it to practical salinity rather than multiplying by 0.001."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The requested global mean SSS involves a weighting choice (volume-weighted over the selected levels versus area-weighted for a surface field), which this fragment constrains.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use `compute_basic_stat` with `op='area_weighted_mean'` and `areacello` for the global and regional SSS means, with weights restricted to the same valid (masked) cells; a plain `mean()` over (y, x) is wrong.",
        "`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default; `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'` for the map correlation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
