      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "Two models are gn (curvilinear) and GFDL-ESM4 is gr (regridded), which affects masks, which operations are exact, and how the model fields are placed on a common grid for the bias and trend maps.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are on native `gn` grids and must be regridded to the WOA23 1° grid for the metrics; GFDL-ESM4 is `gr`, already regridded (conserve_order1) to 1° with a regridded land-sea mask.",
        "Resolution differs (100 km vs 250 km), so features narrower than the coarse grid are not comparable in amplitude."
      ]
